    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51314" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχιορρωγικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥώξ</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with broken hips,
			limping</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέτρον ἰ</span>. an iambic
			trimeter ending in five long syilables ascribed to Ananius, Gramm.
			Harl. in Studemund <i>Ind. Lect. Vratisl.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1887
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				8p.16
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰσχιορρώξ</span></b>  (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στίχος</span>),
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶγος</span>, ὁ,
			Tz.in <i><span class="en">
				<u>An.Ox.</u>
				3.310
			</span></i>.</div>
